=== ROOT CAUSE 2: yabridge elevates its audio thread late ===
  t1:  ts 16.33  yabridge-host.e/audio-0  prio=5   mask=16-31
       ts 17.33  yabridge-host.e/audio-0  prio=85  mask=0-15    <- 200 ms after the burst
yabridge names the thread audio-N at creation but only raises it to SCHED_FIFO 85 when the
host activates the plugin. Until then RT_MIN=50 correctly classifies it as non-audio and
sends it to the E-cores, so the first process() call runs at 4.3 GHz.

Fix: LATE_RT_NAMES='^audio-[0-9]+$' within LATE_RT_PROCS='^yabridge-host\.e$' gets the
P-cores regardless of priority. Scoped deliberately: BGLoading, Disk, worker and
ProcessMonitor in the same process are also FIFO 5 and must stay on the E-cores.

  t2:  ts 13.31  audio-0  prio=5   mask=16-31   born on E-cores
       ts 13.56  audio-0  prio=5   mask=0-15    promoted by name, still FIFO 5
       ts 14.32  audio-0  prio=85  mask=0-15    yabridge raises the priority
  activation burst at ts 14.16 -- after the move. 1.619 -> 0.945 ms (1.71x).

